'ContainerCreating' or events say 'Pulling', simply call this tool again.

Args:
    namespace: Namespace of the Deployment.
    deployment: Name of the Deployment.
    timeout_seconds: Maximum time to wait (30-1800 seconds, default 900)., args: {'namespace': {'title': 'Namespace', 'type': 'string'}, 'deployment': {'title': 'Deployment', 'type': 'string'}, 'timeout_seconds': {'default': 900, 'title': 'Timeout Seconds', 'type': 'integer'}}
k8s_pod_logs_tool: Show recent logs of a Deployment's Pods and the latest namespace events,
to find out why Pods are not Ready or why the application fails.

Args:
    namespace: Namespace of the Deployment.
    deployment: Name of the Deployment.
    tail: Number of log lines to return., args: {'namespace': {'title': 'Namespace', 'type': 'string'}, 'deployment': {'title': 'Deployment', 'type': 'string'}, 'tail': {'default': 40, 'title': 'Tail', 'type': 'integer'}}
k8s_service_check_tool: Check that a Service really works: count its READY endpoints, then open a temporary
kubectl port-forward and send an HTTP GET request. The check only PASSES when the
Service has at least one ready endpoint AND the request returns HTTP 200.

